  "step_3": "The decision reason relies on identifying a sure outcome (100% probability) in either lottery and preferring the one that has it. However, neither lottery has a sure outcome, so the reason cannot apply. Moreover, the individual does not consider certainty or sure outcomes in their reasoning. Instead, they compare the prize amounts under the assumption of similar probabilities. There is no overlap between the information used by the individual (prize size under similar probabilities) and the information required by the decision reason (presence of a sure outcome). The justification provided (favoring higher amount under similar odds) is unrelated to the rule of the decision reason (favoring a sure outcome). Therefore, it is certain that the individual did not use this decision reason.",
